{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_4c51884fdda6e853bdcdf5f72e947d9258551fa29bd2b24101f9020340509661"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors must extend collect_data.py's Q dictionary and row list, update data.csv and data_backup.csv headers, and optionally backfill historical values via API queries."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7ff494c8aa8d0eb39fe5b49a465d09ff02e3b193e91367e3416521b96cf7e316"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: AGENTS.md provides a mandatory step-by-step checklist for onboarding a new agent, described as the single source of truth after earlier omissions caused Jules-related regressions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8664b6228d8e54e27a3b3bf052d7f892f8316f670fa6f775a4b1a5d6c30ff0bd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: generate_chart.py's AGENTS list feeds the README template, GitHub Pages template, and chart toggles, but per-agent sections like percentage lambdas and matplotlib bars are hard-coded and must be duplicated manually."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8f2d2c7459cbe68f7ead6c22dc48793f807fb80e128eb9aadb7d6c6cc998edd0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: derived assets (docs/chart.png, chart-data.json, README.md, docs/index.html) are regenerated by running collect_data.py and generate_chart.py, and generated files must never be hand-edited."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e4e1590e1e908462234f7d9b61d79a00d201246750471613a8122469a758f2b6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: onboarding requires collecting four GitHub search queries per agent (total, merged, ready, draft), verifying each manually in a browser before codifying it."}],"claim_ids":["clm_4c51884fdda6e853bdcdf5f72e947d9258551fa29bd2b24101f9020340509661","clm_7ff494c8aa8d0eb39fe5b49a465d09ff02e3b193e91367e3416521b96cf7e316","clm_8664b6228d8e54e27a3b3bf052d7f892f8316f670fa6f775a4b1a5d6c30ff0bd","clm_8f2d2c7459cbe68f7ead6c22dc48793f807fb80e